  "ecological_interpretation": "Relative colony reproductive performance carries short-lived temporal information about subsequent within-island redistribution after removing island-transition mean growth, prior group size and persistent colony identity. The association remains at the denominator-separated lag-2 endpoint and across frozen sensitivities, but fades by lags 4-5 and provides strong evidence against the predeclared delayed recruitment-echo pattern. This is compatible with short-term performance-linked settlement, retention, or other dynamic local-state processes; colony counts do not identify individual public-information use.",
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Do not claim first evidence of public-information use in Adelie penguins.",
    "Do not call the result a fully preregistered confirmatory test because the V2 provenance repair occurred after observed coefficients were exposed.",
    "Do not interpret the lag-1 association alone mechanistically because predictor and outcome share the predictor-year adult census.",
    "Do not claim a 4-5 year natal recruitment echo; the preregistered contrast is negative.",
    "Do not claim that dynamic state replaces terrain, snow or geomorphology.",
    "Do not infer individual movement or cue use from colony-level counts."
  ]
